From 8642af5aaabb0dbee82abc34d34a4e805eb2dc50 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joshua Bryan <45343084+rafe-walker@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 13:25:50 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 11/11] fix(plugin-mcp): keep array row ids when the same rows
 are sent again (research v2.2)

The update tools declare idempotentHint: true, but Payload gives every array or
blocks row sent without an id a new id. An update that re-sent the rows it
read, without their ids, therefore changed every row id on every call, and
the rows lost their values in other locales (the PAY-06 mechanism).

Before an update by id that carries an array, the stored document is read in
the same locale; a row sent without an id that is identical to the stored row
at the same position (every value it sends equal, every value it leaves out
empty) keeps that row's id (helpers/rowIds.ts). A row that differs or moved is
still a new row, and an id is never given to two rows. A repeat of the same
call with the same ifUpdatedAt is refused as stale, so it changes nothing; a
repeat with the new version keeps the ids. The hint stays.

Tests: rowIds.spec.ts (7).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
